{% doc %}
  Renders either an SVG icon or an uploaded image based on block settings.

  @param {string} icon - The icon name from block.settings.icon
  @param {object} [image_upload] - The uploaded image from block.settings.image_upload
  @param {string} [class_name] - CSS class name for the rendered element
  @param {number} [width] - The width of the icon from block.settings.width
  @param {number} [width_mobile] - The width of the icon from block.settings.width_mobile
  @param {object} [attributes] - Additional HTML attributes to add to the element
  @param {string} [icon_size] - The size of the icon from block.settings.icon_size
  @param {string} [icon_color] - Overrides the SVG icon color; blank inherits the ambient color
{% enddoc %}
{%- comment -%}
  The custom size is built as DECLARATIONS, never as a ready-made `style=`
  attribute, and reaches the icon through `style:` instead of `attributes:`.

  The `icon` snippet writes its OWN `style=` from `icon_color` and prints
  `attributes` right after it. A second `style=` smuggled in through `attributes`
  therefore produced a span with two of them — and HTML keeps the first and
  discards the rest, silently. So picking a colour dropped the size and the icon
  fell back to the 1.6rem default in `.icon--custom-size`; leaving the colour
  blank left only one `style` and it worked. `icon` appends the colour to this
  string, so the two now share one attribute.

  `custom_size_style` is assigned ONLY in custom-size mode, so otherwise it stays
  undefined — nil, which `icon` treats as falsy and skips. Capturing an empty
  string instead would not do: an empty string is TRUTHY in Liquid, and every
  icon in the theme would then carry a bare `style=""`.

  The image branch keeps taking the size as an attribute: that `<div>` has no
  `style` of its own to collide with.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if icon_size == 'custom-size' -%}
  {%- capture custom_size_style -%}
    --icon-custom-size: {{ width | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;--icon-custom-size-mobile: {{ width_mobile | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
  {%- endcapture -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- capture image_attributes -%}
  {{ attributes }}
  {%- if custom_size_style != blank %} style="{{ custom_size_style | strip }}"{% endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if icon != 'none' and image_upload == blank -%}
  {%- render 'icon', icon: icon, attributes: attributes, style: custom_size_style, size: icon_size, icon_color: icon_color, class: class_name -%}
{%- elsif image_upload != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign media_width_desktop = 100
    assign media_width_mobile = 100
    if icon_size == 'custom-size'
      assign media_width_desktop = width
      assign media_width_mobile = width_mobile
    endif
  -%}
  {%- capture image_sizes -%}(min-width: 768px) {{ media_width_desktop }}px, {{ media_width_mobile }}px{%- endcapture -%}
  <div class="icon icon--{{ icon_size }} icon--image" {{ image_attributes }}>
    {%- liquid
      # Guarantee the alt ATTRIBUTE exists: with no alt text image_tag omits it
      # entirely, which axe/Lighthouse fails. Empty alt = decorative, the safe default.
      assign image_upload_alt = image_upload.alt | default: ''
    -%}
    {{ image_upload | image_url: width: image_upload.width | image_tag: sizes: image_sizes, widths: '100, 200, 300, 400', class: class_name, alt: image_upload_alt }}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
